  {
    "title": "Musical Improv: An Introduction | Workshop by Improv Lore",
    "excerpt": "If you’ve ever thought, “I’m not musical enough for musical improv,” this workshop is for you. \nMusical improv isn’t about having a perfect singing voice; it’s about listening, storytelling, pattern recognition, and &hellip;",
    "full_content": "If you’ve ever thought, “I’m not musical enough for musical improv,” this workshop is for you.\nMusical improv isn’t about having a perfect singing voice; it’s about listening, storytelling, pattern recognition, and play. In this workshop, we’ll explore some simple musical concepts, experiment with rhyme and rhythm, learn a few useful song structures, and practise turning scenes into songs without overthinking them.\nWe’ll play musical games, build choruses and verses, and explore a few classic musical improv formats like the Irish Drinking Song, and the Hoedown along the way.\nNo musical experience required. Just bring your curiosity, your willingness to sing badly before you sing brilliantly, and your sense of play.",
