  {
    "title": "Improv 101: How Not to Panic on Stage | Workshop by Improv Lore",
    "excerpt": "Most people think improvisers are fearless; the truth is they’ve just learnt what to do when they don’t know what to do. \nThis beginner-friendly introduction to improv is designed for anyone who’s ever worried about &hellip;",
    "full_content": "Most people think improvisers are fearless; the truth is they’ve just learnt what to do when they don’t know what to do.\nThis beginner-friendly introduction to improv is designed for anyone who’s ever worried about saying the wrong thing, running out of ideas, or freezing up in front of others. Through fun games, simple exercises, and guided scene work, you’ll learn how to trust your instincts, embrace uncertainty, and stay present when things don’t go according to plan.\nThrough the course, we’ll explore some core principles of improvisation, collaborative storytelling, and spontaneous creativity in a supportive, low-stake environment.\nNo acting or stage experience required. You don’t need to be funny, quick-witted, or confident. You just need a willingness to step on stage and discover that you can handle more than you think.",
